# PR Babysitting

When the user asks the agent to create a pull request, after the PR is created:

- Start babysitting that PR automatically unless the user explicitly asks not to.
- Pull the latest branch state, then check unresolved GitHub review comments, CodeRabbit comments, mergeability, and CI status.
- Fix valid actionable comments that are clearly within the scope of the PR.
- Push scoped fixes to the PR branch, then continue babysitting because new commits can trigger fresh CI and review comments.
- Keep monitoring on a short loop until the PR is merge-ready and CodeRabbit's updated review comment explicitly says there are no actionable comments, or until the user asks to stop. Do not rely on CodeRabbit's status check alone.
- If CodeRabbit says review is paused or rate-limited, do not add a GitHub Actions scheduler. Use a Cursor loop for that PR, wait until the retry window expires, then comment `@coderabbitai review` once.
- Report comments that are ambiguous, invalid, unrelated to the PR, or require product/owner approval instead of guessing.

Do not merge the PR unless the user explicitly asks.
